<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of use - BornTask"
  description="The rules for using BornTask."
  canonical="https://www.borntask.com/terms/"
  otherHref="/privacy/"
  otherLabel="Privacy notice"
>
  <header>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="intro">The rules for using BornTask. By signing in or creating a workspace you agree to these terms.</p>
    <p class="meta">Last updated 16 October 2026</p>
  </header>
  <section>
    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>BornTask is software for planning and tracking work: projects, tasks, comments, files, workflow rules, invitations, search, and optional integrations (Google Chat, GitHub, Asana import, MCP and personal API tokens). We host it at app.borntask.com. Features may change as we ship.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Who may use it</h2>
    <p>You must be able to form a contract and, if you are signing in for an organisation, have authority to bind that organisation. You sign in with Google or Microsoft. A first sign-in with no workspace lets you create one. Invitations add teammates and guests.</p>
    <p>Workspace owners and admins control who may join, which sign-in providers are allowed, and guest invites. You must keep your account and tokens to yourself.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Your content and responsibility</h2>
    <p>You (and your workspace) own the content you put in BornTask. You grant us a limited licence to host, display, back up and transmit that content so the product works, including through integrations you switch on.</p>
    <p>You must have the right to upload what you upload. Do not use BornTask for unlawful content, malware, or to infringe other people's rights. Workflow rules, comments and @mentions are visible to people with access to that project.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not probe, scrape or overload the service beyond normal product use.</li>
      <li>Do not bypass tenant isolation, workflow rules or permission checks.</li>
      <li>Do not share personal API tokens or session cookies.</li>
      <li>Do not use MCP or tokens to take actions the signed-in user could not take in the app. MCP cannot delete tasks, change settings or invite people.</li>
      <li>Respect the people you invite and the data in shared projects.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Integrations</h2>
    <p>Optional connections (Google Chat, GitHub, email via SendGrid, MCP clients) are provided as-is and depend on those providers. We are not responsible for outages or policy changes on their side. You can disconnect Chat, revoke GitHub, revoke tokens and turn email events off in settings. Creating tasks from Chat still follows the same move rules as the app.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Price</h2>
    <p>The published price is €1 per paid member per month plus VAT. Owners, admins, members and viewers count; guests are free. Card collection is not connected yet; when it is, owners and admins will manage it under Billing. People added mid-month are charged for the remaining days; removals are credited on the next invoice.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>We aim to keep BornTask available but do not promise uninterrupted service. We may modify or withdraw features. Planned maintenance and incidents will be handled as reasonably as we can.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>The service is provided as-is. To the extent allowed by Maltese and EU law we are not liable for lost profits, lost data you can restore from your own copies, or indirect loss. Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or any liability that cannot be limited by law. If a cap applies, it is the fees paid for the workspace in the three months before the claim.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Suspension and closure</h2>
    <p>We may suspend an account that breaches these terms or threatens the service. You may stop using BornTask at any time. A workspace owner may delete the workspace; deletion completes after 30 days. We may delete unused or abusive workspaces after notice where we can reach an owner.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Malta. Courts of Malta have jurisdiction, without limiting any mandatory consumer protection rights you have in your EU member state. The EU privacy notice is at <a href="/privacy/">www.borntask.com/privacy</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top will change. Continued use after a material update means you accept the new terms, except where the law requires a clearer agreement.</p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
